<title>FINLAND: FINNISH SDP RETAINS LEAD, CENTRE PARTY NOW 2ND - POLL.</title>
<headline>FINNISH SDP RETAINS LEAD, CENTRE PARTY NOW 2ND - POLL.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1997-03-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Finland's biggest political</p>
<p>party, the Social Democrats, retained its lead in an opinion</p>
<p>poll in February, Finnish radio news reported at the weekend.</p>
<p>The opposition Centre Party overtook the conservatives for</p>
<p>second place. The monthly survey was made by polling institute</p>
<p>Taloustutkimus Oy among some 1,900 people.</p>
<p>(Previous surveys also by Taloustutkimus, figs in pct):</p>
<p>			Feb    Jan    Dec   Election '96  Election '95</p>
<p> SDP		  24.8   24.8   25.3	24.5	    28.3</p>
<p> Centre Party     21.7   20.2   20.0	21.8	    19.8</p>
<p> Conservatives    20.4   21.2   19.7	21.6	    17.9</p>
<p> Green Party	10.3    9.8   11.8	 6.3	     6.5</p>
<p> Leftist Alliance  9.1    9.1    7.7	10.4	    11.2</p>
<p> Swedish Party     4.1    4.7    5.1	 5.5	     5.1</p>
<p> Young Finns	 3.4    3.7    3.9	 1.3	     2.8</p>
<p> Christian League  3.0    3.3    3.0	 3.2	     3.0</p>
<p> Perussuomalaiset  1.0    1.0    1.0	 0.9	     1.3</p>
<p>NOTE -- Election '96 is local government election held in</p>
<p>October last year and Election '95 is parliament election held</p>
<p>in March 1995. The next general election is due in March 1999.</p>
<p>--Helsinki newsroom +358-9-680 50 245, e-mail news@reuters.fi</p>
</text>
